import ../../../testing/driver.dl
import ../../../ui/source_transactions.dl

document example:
    editor "Source" containing "😀 alpha\nbeta" using no UI appearance

to get [a transaction test edit at row] {integer:row} [from] {integer:first} [through] {integer:last} [inserting] {string:text}:
    return a JSON object containing [JSON child "range" is (an LSP range from line row and character first to line row and character last), JSON text "newText" is text]

to get [transaction test changes for] {string:uri}:
    return a JSON object containing [JSON child "changes" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child uri is (a JSON array containing [a transaction test edit at row 2 from 0 through 4 inserting "B", a transaction test edit at row 1 from 3 through 8 inserting "A"])])]

set instance to an instance of example
set window to the address of instance
set view to a UI view of window sized 700 by 500 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
set workspace to a UI source workspace in window rooted at "file:///workspace"
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set editor to the UI source editor labeled "Source" in workspace
set main to editor's document
set files to a new JSON-RPC object
configure UI source document main named "main.dl" at "file:///workspace/main.dl" prefixed by "# hidden\n" using UI CPU analysis with files files
free files
restore UI source location (editor's current) in editor in (the address of view)
set view's selection's anchor to 5
set view's selection's caret to 15
set original to main's source
set payload to transaction test changes for (main's uri)
set transaction to a UI source transaction applying payload for editor in (the address of view)
free payload
require condition ((transaction's succeeded) and (main's source = original)) reporting "Preparing a source transaction changed its model."
require condition (commit UI source transaction (the address of transaction) in (the address of view)) reporting "A valid source transaction was rejected."
require condition (main's source = "😀 A\nB") reporting "A source transaction lost Unicode or unordered edits."
require condition (view's selection's caret = 8) reporting "A source transaction did not map its caret through all edits."
set value to the UI value for (editor's node) in window
require condition ((value's undo != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text edit)) and (value's undo's next = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text edit))) reporting "A source transaction was split into several undo operations."
queue UI input of kind 3 key 90 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 2 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
synchronize UI source workspace workspace at 1.0 seconds
require condition ((main's source = original) and ((view's selection's anchor = 5) and (view's selection's caret = 15))) reporting "Undo did not restore the source transaction's original text and selection."
free UI source transaction (the address of transaction)

set imported to a UI source document named "helper.dl" at "file:///lib/helper.dl" containing "# helper" in (main's project)
set view's selection's anchor and view's selection's caret to 7
visit UI source document imported selecting 0 through 0 in editor in (the address of view)
set source to view's selection's caret source
set payload to transaction test changes for (main's uri)
set transaction to a UI source transaction applying payload for editor in (the address of view)
free payload
require condition (commit UI source transaction (the address of transaction) in (the address of view)) reporting "A parked writable source could not receive a transaction."
require condition ((editor's document = imported) and ((view's selection's caret source = source) and (view's selection's caret = 0))) reporting "Editing a parked source moved the imported view's selection."
require condition ((the UI value for (editor's node) in window)'s text = "# helper") reporting "A parked source transaction replaced its imported view."
show UI source document main in editor in (the address of view)
require condition ((main's source = "😀 A\nB") and (view's selection's caret = 6)) reporting "A parked source lost its committed text or mapped caret."
queue UI input of kind 3 key 90 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 2 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
synchronize UI source workspace workspace at 2.0 seconds
require condition (main's source = original) reporting "A parked source transaction could not be undone after returning."
free UI source transaction (the address of transaction)

set payload to transaction test changes for (main's uri)
set changes to the JSON member named "changes" in payload
add JSON-RPC member (imported's uri) containing (a JSON array containing [a transaction test edit at row 0 from 0 through 1 inserting "changed"]) to changes
set transaction to a UI source transaction applying payload for editor in (the address of view)
free payload
require condition ((transaction's succeeded = false) and (main's source = original)) reporting "A read-only target partially applied its other source edits."
require condition ((commit UI source transaction (the address of transaction) in (the address of view)) = false) reporting "An invalid source transaction was committed."
free UI source transaction (the address of transaction)

set payload to a JSON object containing [JSON child "changes" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child (main's uri) is (a JSON array containing [a transaction test edit at row 2 from 0 through 4 inserting "B", a transaction test edit at row 0 from 0 through 8 inserting "protected"])])]
set transaction to a UI source transaction applying payload for editor in (the address of view)
free payload
require condition ((transaction's succeeded = false) and (main's source = original)) reporting "An edit of hidden context partially changed the visible source."
free UI source transaction (the address of transaction)

set payload to transaction test changes for (main's uri)
set transaction to a UI source transaction applying payload for editor in (the address of view)
free payload
set UI text of (editor's node) in window to "new source"
require condition ((commit UI source transaction (the address of transaction) in (the address of view)) = false) reporting "An obsolete transaction overwrote newer control text."
require condition ((the UI value for (editor's node) in window)'s text = "new source") reporting "Rejecting an obsolete transaction discarded the user's edit."
free UI source transaction (the address of transaction)
load UI main source of editor in (the address of view) from original at 3.0 seconds

set model to the UI language model for main in (workspace's client)
set model's opened to true
set model's version to 3
set model's snapshot to main's prefix + main's source
set first to a JSON object containing [JSON child "textDocument" is (a JSON object containing [JSON text "uri" is (main's uri), JSON number "version" is 3]), JSON child "edits" is (a JSON array containing [a transaction test edit at row 1 from 3 through 8 inserting "A"])]
set second to a JSON object containing [JSON child "textDocument" is (a JSON object containing [JSON text "uri" is (main's uri), JSON number "version" is 4]), JSON child "edits" is (a JSON array containing [a transaction test edit at row 2 from 0 through 4 inserting "B"])]
set payload to a JSON object containing [JSON child "documentChanges" is (a JSON array containing [first, second])]
set transaction to a UI source transaction applying payload for editor in (the address of view)
free payload
require condition (commit UI source transaction (the address of transaction) in (the address of view)) reporting "Ordered versioned source edits did not advance their virtual document version."
require condition (main's source = "😀 A\nB") reporting "Ordered source edits did not use the preceding text snapshot."
require condition (value's undo's next = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text edit)) reporting "Ordered changes for one source created separate undo records."
free UI source transaction (the address of transaction)
set model's version to 8
set model's snapshot to main's prefix + main's source
set request to a JSON object containing [JSON child "textDocument" is (a JSON object containing [JSON text "uri" is (main's uri), JSON number "version" is 7]), JSON child "edits" is (a JSON array containing [a transaction test edit at row 2 from 0 through 1 inserting "old version"])]
set payload to a JSON object containing [JSON child "documentChanges" is (a JSON array containing [request])]
set transaction to a UI source transaction applying payload for editor in (the address of view)
free payload
require condition ((transaction's succeeded = false) and (main's source = "😀 A\nB")) reporting "An obsolete document version was accepted."
free UI source transaction (the address of transaction)
set payload to a JSON object containing [JSON child "changes" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child (main's uri) is (a JSON array containing [a transaction test edit at row 2 from 0 through 1 inserting "locked"])])]
set transaction to a UI source transaction applying payload for editor in (the address of view)
free payload
set UI control (editor's node) read only true in window
require condition ((commit UI source transaction (the address of transaction) in (the address of view)) = false) reporting "Committing a prepared transaction bypassed a newer read-only policy."
free UI source transaction (the address of transaction)
set payload to a JSON object containing [JSON child "changes" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child (main's uri) is (a JSON array containing [a transaction test edit at row 2 from 0 through 1 inserting "locked"])])]
set transaction to a UI source transaction applying payload for editor in (the address of view)
free payload
require condition ((transaction's succeeded = false) and (main's source = "😀 A\nB")) reporting "A source transaction bypassed the application's read-only policy."
free UI source transaction (the address of transaction)
free UI source workspace workspace
close the address of view
close window
print line "Source transactions stage Unicode edits atomically, protect context and imports, preserve parked undo, and validate source versions."
